Fix a crash (SIGBUS) when the macOS 26+ accessibility stack queries the
editor's text with an out-of-range or empty range.

QsciAccessibleScintillaBase::textRange() creates a QByteArray sized from
the position range without validating it.  The macOS accessibility
bridge can pass degenerate or reversed offsets, producing a range where
end <= start.  The resulting empty QByteArray's data() points at shared
read-only storage inside QtCore, and SCI_GETTEXTRANGE writes its NUL
terminator through it: EXC_BAD_ACCESS / KERN_PROTECTION_FAILURE.

See https://github.com/openscad/openscad/issues/6933

diff -ru QScintilla_src-2.14.1/src/SciAccessibility.cpp QScintilla_src-2.14.1-fixed/src/SciAccessibility.cpp
--- QScintilla_src-2.14.1/src/SciAccessibility.cpp
+++ QScintilla_src-2.14.1-fixed/src/SciAccessibility.cpp
@@ -354,6 +354,13 @@
 QString QsciAccessibleScintillaBase::textRange(QsciScintillaBase *sb,
         int start_position, int end_position)
 {
+    // Reject invalid or empty ranges, eg. from degenerate or reversed
+    // offsets in an accessibility query.  Otherwise the QByteArray below
+    // would be empty and data() would return a pointer to shared read-only
+    // storage, which SCI_GETTEXTRANGE then writes through.
+    if (start_position < 0 || end_position <= start_position)
+        return QString();
+
     QByteArray bytes(end_position - start_position + 1, '\0');

     sb->SendScintilla(QsciScintillaBase::SCI_GETTEXTRANGE, start_position,
